<!-- AI agent handoff. Vars: apiUrl, serviceId, apiKey (may be absent) -->
<div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-2xl border-2 border-blue-500 dark:border-blue-500 shadow-lg overflow-hidden mb-6">
  <div class="p-6 sm:p-8">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;">
      <svg style="width: 24px; height: 24px; min-width: 24px;" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path>
      </svg>
      <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 0;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;" class="mb-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Let an AI agent set this up</h2>
          <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">Recommended</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4 text-sm">
          Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and anything else that can read your repo.
          It detects your project, writes or updates your pipelines, and opens a pull request
          you review before anything merges.
          {{#unless apiKey}}
          <span class="block mt-2 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
            Your API key is only shown once, when the service is created. Mint a new one in
            <a href="/settings/api-keys" class="underline">Settings → API keys</a> and paste it into the prompt below.
          </span>
          {{/unless}}
        </p>

        <div class="relative">
          <div class="bg-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-950 rounded-xl p-4 font-mono text-xs text-green-400 overflow-x-auto">
<pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap"><code id="ai_agent_prompt">Set up GitLaunch CI/CD in this repository.

Follow the skill at {{apiUrl}}/skills/gitlaunch-onboarding/SKILL.md
(fetch it and its references/ files, then follow it exactly).

GitLaunch host: {{apiUrl}}
Service ID:     {{serviceId}}
API key:        {{#if apiKey}}{{apiKey}}{{else}}&lt;paste your API key&gt;{{/if}}

Detect my project type and whether I already have CI/CD. If I don't,
generate pipelines with GitLaunch build reporting and deploy control
built in. If I do, integrate GitLaunch into what's already there.
Open a pull request — don't commit to my default branch.</code></pre>
          </div>
          <button onclick="copyText('ai_agent_prompt')"
            class="absolute top-3 right-3 px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white text-xs font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors">
            Copy prompt
          </button>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          This prompt contains your API key — paste it into your own coding agent, not into a shared chat.
          This page advances on its own as soon as your first build reaches GitLaunch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
  <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700"></div>
  <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500">or set it up by hand</span>
  <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700"></div>
</div>
